Short:        Small version control system for OS3
Author:       Ronny Krueger
Uploader:     Ronny Krueger
Type:         dev/misc
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     MUI 3.8 (GUI); TCP/IP + AmiSSL 5 for clone/push/pull
Distribution: Aminet
Replaces:     dev/misc/AmiVCS.lha

AmiVCS is a small, deliberately simple version control system for
AmigaOS 3.x: commits, branches, staging and three-way merge, all local.
An AmiVCS server is only needed for clone, push and pull; it also offers
a web interface for browsing repositories, history and diffs.

  amivcs        command line client
  amivcs-gui    MUI front end (history graph, staging, diffs)
  AMIVCSPrefs   settings editor (server, user, author name)

The same programs (command line and a Qt GUI) exist for macOS, Linux and
Windows; the server (PHP) is part of the source distribution.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive and double-click "Install-AmiVCS" (Commodore
Installer, part of OS 3.2 in SYS:System). Without the Installer, use the
shell script instead:  CD AmiVCS  and  Execute Install-AmiVCS.shell
Existing settings are never overwritten.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.x, 68000 or better, no FPU needed
- MUI 3.8 or newer for amivcs-gui
- for clone/push/pull only: TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library,
  AmiSSL 5 and an AmiVCS server

Documentation and user interface are in German.
Die Dokumentation (Docs/AmiVCS.guide) und die Programme sind deutsch.

